        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Let a random variable is uniformly distributed over [a, b] with expectation and variance\ne and v respectively. Find the value of ab."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Give an expression in the stated parameters."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "short_answer",
      "acceptable_answers": [
        "e^2-3*v",
        "e^2-3v",
        "e**2-3*v"
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "For Uniform[a,b], e=(a+b)/2 and v=(b−a)²/12. Therefore ab=((a+b)²−(b−a)²)/4=e²−3v."
        }
      ]
    },
